{"authored" [{"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14\\cdot 1-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(14x-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[14\\pi -\\frac{5}{3}{\\pi }^{3}]-[14\\cdot 0-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}] \\\\  & =14\\pi -\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})={sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-477.json" "file_sha256" "33a6fb5067d0a9efaf01c1f5cedcb1ea3a49856e6344dcc1c050d26e6b496184" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-477.json" "file_sha256" "33a6fb5067d0a9efaf01c1f5cedcb1ea3a49856e6344dcc1c050d26e6b496184" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-478.json" "file_sha256" "5aa058c8db4b888fa28de731cf2c707eac712f54c3919fed45d4e65cb913a59a" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-478.json" "file_sha256" "5aa058c8db4b888fa28de731cf2c707eac712f54c3919fed45d4e65cb913a59a" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-479.json" "file_sha256" "39c8e5a4f8461de8bb14161ec0e580a0d969324edd6bf19157b6e231fc7ee934" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-479.json" "file_sha256" "39c8e5a4f8461de8bb14161ec0e580a0d969324edd6bf19157b6e231fc7ee934" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-480.json" "file_sha256" "6d7fc04f1faa3094ccb11ab419906960d3c2515446565e5b1d0a57f11ed2bf6f" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-480.json" "file_sha256" "6d7fc04f1faa3094ccb11ab419906960d3c2515446565e5b1d0a57f11ed2bf6f" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-114353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-114353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14\\cdot 1-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(14x-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[14\\pi -\\frac{5}{3}{\\pi }^{3}]-[14\\cdot 0-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}] \\\\  & =14\\pi -\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡x=1-{cos}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({csc}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-114350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.$ \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}=\\frac{1}{-{sin}^{2}⁡x}=-{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-49446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are using the identity\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-49325" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49325" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}-2"] ["math" "6-2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{3}-6"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}+6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49325" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-114435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}-1"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}+1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-114423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-73526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-10565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-10565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4({sec}^{2}⁡x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{sec}^{2}⁡x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (-3{x}^{2}+4{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-10565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-10565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-10565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-{x}^{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-{x}^{3}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-10565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3({cot}^{2}⁡x+1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3({cot}^{2}⁡x+1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+3\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-73513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{3}+1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}+2"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-2"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}-3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-x)\\,{|}_{1}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =({(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-({1}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-352709" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352709" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-362808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}-{cot}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-362808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}-{cot}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{({csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x)+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})\\,{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{e-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+(\\sqrt{e-1})^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+(1)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+e-1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1)-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-362808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-362808" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-362808" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1-\\ln(2)}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-73518" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73518" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{cos}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{sin}^{2}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-73518" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =[-0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-114441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "4(\\pi -2)"] ["math" "4-\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1"] ["math" "\\pi -3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine $\\int \\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =5x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)={csc}^{2}⁡(5x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{[{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)+1]\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{csc}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡(5x-2)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)\\text{d}x & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-114510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x-2)+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+C"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x-2)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-114510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})={sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ {tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\text{d}x & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\text{d}x-\\int 1\\cdot \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c15144e6a99feb7c06ddce219e48d16d26aa9d46527e66c83a77c81d177dfa44"} {"question" "q-49268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039502/state.json" "file_sha256" "8979bec965fc1baba21a7f08ac71c63b309dd8b2f25d6bd29bb0054459a34af3"} {"question" "q-49268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "